      "role": "user",
      "content": "Two Sum\n\nGiven an array of integers nums and an integer target, return the indices of the two numbers that add up to target. Exactly one solution exists, and you may not use the same element twice. Return the answer in any order.\n\nExample: nums = [2,7,11,15], target = 9 -> [0,1]\nConstraints: 2 <= len(nums) <= 10^4, -10^9 <= nums[i], target <= 10^9.",
      "id": "m-0",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-07T06:09:02.794Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "analysis",
      "content": "Edge cases to cover before submitting: empty input, single element, and the all-duplicates case.\n\nKey invariant: the data structure state after processing prefix i fully determines the answer for i+1.\n\nComplexity check: one pass, O(n) time, O(n) auxiliary space for the map. That meets the constraint.",
      "id": "m-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-07T06:09:03.159Z",
      "durationMs": 3932,
      "stepIndex": 1
    },
